ted_from_span":null}},"source_text":"fn chunks_vectored<'a>(&'a self, dst: &mut [IoSlice<'a>]) -> usize {\n        if dst.is_empty() {\n            return 0;\n        }\n\n        if self.has_remaining() {\n            dst[0] = IoSlice::new(self.chunk());\n            1\n        } else {\n            0\n        }\n    }","attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Fills `dst` with potentially multiple slices starting at `self`'s"},{"DocComment":" current position."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If the `Buf` is backed by disjoint slices of bytes, `chunk_vectored` enables"},{"DocComment":" fetching more than one slice at once. `dst` is a slice of `IoSlice`"},{"DocComment":" references, enabling the slice to be directly used with [`writev`]"},{"DocComment":" without any further conversion. The sum of the lengths of all the"},{"DocComment":" buffers written to `dst` will be less than or equal to `Buf::remaining()`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The entries in `dst` will be overwritten, but the data **contained** by"},{"DocComment":" the slices **will not** be modified. The return value is the number of"},{"DocComment":" slices written to `dst`. If `Buf::remaining()` is non-zero, then this"},{"DocComment":" writes at least one non-empty slice to `dst`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This is a lower level function. Most operations are done with other"},{"DocComment":" functions."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Implementer notes"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This function should never panic. Once the end of the buffer is reached,"},{"DocComment":" i.e., `Buf::remaining` returns 0, calls to `chunk_vectored` must return 0"},{"DocComment":" without mutating `dst`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Implementations should also take care to properly handle being called"},{"DocComment":" with `dst` being a zero length slice."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`writev`]: http://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/readv.2.html"}],"inline":null,"rename":null